From: burakgon <burakgon12@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915/display: Pin ASUS ExpertBook Ultra B9406CAA to PSR1

The Samsung ATNA40LE01 OLED in the ASUS ExpertBook Ultra B9406CAA (Panther
Lake, PCI subsystem 0x1043:0x15e4, sink OUI 00:aa:01) advertises Panel
Replay Selective Update with Early Transport over a DSC link, which is what
the driver picks by default. On this panel that mode:

  - logs "Timed out waiting PSR idle state", "[CRTC:151:pipe A] DSB 0 poll
    error" and "CPU pipe A FIFO underrun" with visible corruption (7.2.0);
  - flickers, and smears with VRR enabled (7.2.4);
  - comes up desaturated after every HDR-enabling modeset and leaves stale
    content on screen (7.2.2); dropping only Early Transport keeps the
    washed-out colors and slows the cursor to ~20 fps.

Disabling Panel Replay alone is not enough: the driver then falls back to
PSR2 selective update over the DSC link, and every update paints red/green
garbage. PSR1 is clean across all of the above, and self-refresh still
saves power on a static screen.

Apply both existing quirks to this machine, QUIRK_DISABLE_EDP_PANEL_REPLAY
for the panel and QUIRK_DISABLE_PSR2 for the platform, which leaves PSR1.
This is what owners run today with xe.enable_panel_replay=0 plus
xe.enable_psr=1 (or xe.enable_psr2_sel_fetch=0) on the kernel command line;
the quirks scope it to this laptop instead of changing the defaults
globally.

Tested with the equivalent module parameters on several B9406CAA units,
Linux 7.1.6 to 7.2.8. The quirk entries themselves have not yet been tested
in a built kernel.

Link: https://github.com/burakgon/asus-expertbook-linux/issues/7
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_quirks.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_quirks.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_quirks.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_quirks.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_quirks.c
@@ -262,6 +262,9 @@
 
 	/* Xiaomi Book Pro 14 2026 */
 	{ 0xb081, 0x1d72, 0x2424, quirk_disable_psr2 },
+
+	/* ASUS ExpertBook Ultra B9406CAA */
+	{ 0xb080, 0x1043, 0x15e4, quirk_disable_psr2 },
 };
 
 static const struct intel_dpcd_quirk intel_dpcd_quirks[] = {
@@ -289,6 +292,14 @@
 		.sink_oui = SINK_OUI(0x00, 0x22, 0xb9),
 		.hook = quirk_disable_edp_panel_replay,
 	},
+	/* ASUS ExpertBook Ultra B9406CAA, Samsung ATNA40LE01 OLED */
+	{
+		.device = DEVICE_ID_ANY,
+		.subsystem_vendor = 0x1043,
+		.subsystem_device = 0x15e4,
+		.sink_oui = SINK_OUI(0x00, 0xaa, 0x01),
+		.hook = quirk_disable_edp_panel_replay,
+	},
 };
 
 void intel_init_quirks(struct intel_display *display)
